codemap 9
tour feature-remove-tour
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note The document toolbar's 'delete tour' removes the tour being read from the map. The reader reaches for it to retire a tour while reading the map, without switching to the CLI (deleting is in the document). The status bar names it and its step count, the document empties, and the map is marked unsaved until it is saved. A tour that other tours link to is refused: the status bar names the linking steps and nothing changes. It sits in the menu at the end of the toolbar (the ellipsis button, then 'delete tour'). A run at 1600x1000 before this showed the toolbar as one row of six identical bracketed buttons, 'delete tour' last beside 'expand all': a removal with no undo drawn at the weight of the view buttons it sits next to. In the menu it takes two deliberate presses and is a danger row that fires only once the pointer has moved onto it. Nothing codemap had answered it: tour-rm in the Console is a command the reader in the document does not type, a confirm dialog would be the window's only modal box (feature-build-tour rejected a dialog because it blocks the window and needed a ui change to stop clicks beneath it), and undo is deferred by the owner. The menu is built once (Frame::menu) because the toolbars' less used actions have nowhere else to go; this is its first item. The owner asked for one design built, not several prototypes.

